 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.48,
   "text": "Hey, welcome back to the studio."
  },
  {
   "start": 2.68,
   "end": 7.71,
   "text": "Today we're making soy candles at home, and it's easier than it looks."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.03,
   "end": 15.24,
   "text": "A lot of you asked me, what if the wax gets too hot, or the candle comes out lumpy?"
  },
  {
   "start": 15.68,
   "end": 19.62,
   "text": "Honestly, I was scared of it too the first time."
  },
  {
   "start": 19.82,
   "end": 27.76,
   "text": "But with a thermometer, a steady pour and a little patience, it's one of the most beginner friendly crafts out there."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.08,
   "end": 31.65,
   "text": "Everything we need today comes in the Pour Kit."
  },
  {
   "start": 32.09,
   "end": 37.48,
   "text": "Soy wax flakes, cotton wicks, a pouring pitcher, a thermometer and four fragrance oils."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.68,
   "end": 40.89,
   "text": "Before we start, a quick word on safety."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.21,
   "end": 46.24,
   "text": "Always melt the wax in a double boiler, never directly on the burner."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.68,
   "end": 53.53,
   "text": "Keep the handle dry, keep kids and pets away from the stove, and never leave melting wax alone."
  },
  {
   "start": 53.73,
   "end": 56.21,
   "text": "First project, a classic jar candle."
  },
  {
   "start": 56.53,
   "end": 63.01,
   "text": "Fill the pitcher about halfway with wax flakes and set it inside a pot of simmering water."
  },
  {
   "start": 63.45,
   "end": 68.11,
   "text": "Stir gently until everything is clear and the thermometer reads 85 degrees."
  },
  {
   "start": 68.31,
   "end": 75.52,
   "text": "While it melts, stick a wick to the bottom of the jar and center it with the wooden clip."
  },
  {
   "start": 75.84,
   "end": 82.69,
   "text": "Now take the pitcher off the heat and add the fragrance oil, about 10% of the wax weight."
  },
  {
   "start": 83.13,
   "end": 88.52,
   "text": "Stir slowly for two full minutes, so the scent really binds with the wax."
  },
  {
   "start": 88.72,
   "end": 93.75,
   "text": "Let it cool down to 60 degrees and pour in one steady stream."
  },
  {
   "start": 94.07,
   "end": 99.46,
   "text": "Leave about a centimeter at the top and let it set for four hours."
  },
  {
   "start": 99.9,
   "end": 100.93,
   "text": "That's it!"
  },
  {
   "start": 101.13,
   "end": 103.61,
   "text": "Look at that smooth, creamy top."
  },
  {
   "start": 103.93,
   "end": 107.87,
   "text": "Simple, right? And the whole room already smells like vanilla."
  },
  {
   "start": 108.31,
   "end": 111.52,
   "text": "Next, let's make something you can give away."
  },
  {
   "start": 111.72,
   "end": 114.2,
   "text": "A two-tone candle, poured in layers."
  },
  {
   "start": 114.52,
   "end": 121.37,
   "text": "I'm adding a few chips of terracotta dye to the bottom layer and leaving the top one natural."
  },
  {
   "start": 121.81,
   "end": 128.29,
   "text": "Pour the first layer, then wait about 30 minutes until the surface is firm but still warm."
  },
  {
   "start": 128.49,
   "end": 134.61,
   "text": "If the timing feels too hard, just touch the surface: it should feel like soft butter."
  },
  {
   "start": 134.93,
   "end": 141.05,
   "text": "Now the natural layer goes on top, nice and slow, over the back of a spoon."
  },
  {
   "start": 141.49,
   "end": 145.43,
   "text": "The line between the two colors turned out perfectly straight."
  },
  {
   "start": 145.63,
   "end": 149.93,
   "text": "A ribbon and a handwritten tag, and it's ready to wrap."
  },
  {
   "start": 150.25,
   "end": 154.91,
   "text": "For the last idea, let's give an old teacup a second life."
  },
  {
   "start": 155.35,
   "end": 161.47,
   "text": "This one was hiding in the back of my cupboard with a chip on the rim."
  },
  {
   "start": 161.67,
   "end": 164.88,
   "text": "Same wax, same wick, just a smaller pour."
  },
  {
   "start": 165.2,
   "end": 169.5,
   "text": "Here, a few bumps on top are part of the charm."
  },
  {
   "start": 169.94,
   "end": 172.79,
   "text": "Mismatched cups make the best candles anyway."
  },
  {
   "start": 172.99,
   "end": 178.74,
   "text": "Once all three are set, let them cure for 48 hours before you light them."
  },
  {
   "start": 179.06,
   "end": 183.72,
   "text": "Trim each wick to about six millimeters, and now it lights up."
  },
  {
   "start": 184.16,
   "end": 187.37,
   "text": "And here they are, our three finished candles."
  },
  {
   "start": 187.57,
   "end": 191.87,
   "text": "Anyone can make these in one evening with the Pour Kit."
  },
  {
   "start": 192.19,
   "end": 195.76,
   "text": "And the same method works for almost any container."
  },
  {
   "start": 196.2,
   "end": 199.77,
   "text": "Tins, teacups, coconut shells, even an old sugar bowl."
  },
  {
   "start": 199.97,
   "end": 202.45,
   "text": "So, still afraid of hot wax?"
  },
  {
   "start": 202.77,
   "end": 207.07,
   "text": "Tell us in the comments which scent we should try next."
  },
  {
   "start": 207.51,
   "end": 211.08,
   "text": "And subscribe to keep your next weekend project easy."
  },
  {
   "start": 211.28,
   "end": 212.31,
   "text": "Happy pouring!"
  }
 ],
